. Part of the same Task C change; AI assistance is recorded in the final Developer Guide.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":64,"deletions":1},"test-code":{"insertions":68,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"4f9503914367697eb15cd47eb4935cf297cd7189","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Document the v1.3 next-session workflow","messageBody":"Explain booking formats, validation, replacement, persistence, card states, and shifting displayed indices in the User Guide. Align the scheduling use case with the submitted MVP and cite AI assistance in the Developer Guide.\n\nRefs #57. Part of the same Task C change; AI assistance is recorded in the final Developer Guide.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":56,"deletions":5}}}]},{"date":"2026-10-15T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"e828d8052a61d2716fca63370056768e6760b868","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge remote-tracking branch \u0027upstream/master\u0027 into codex/add-next-session-model","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"9aa986cabcc3250443447da12ab7263133ad15c4","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Remove the unused record-date parsing helper","messageBody":"Keep Task C focused on next-session booking. The measurement and performance owners can introduce their shared date helper with their callers and tests. Addresses review feedback on PR #58.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":0,"deletions":13},"test-code":{"insertions":0,"deletions":13}}},{"hash":"14a1f3683343bc174daadca1126703b7875ea6c9","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Distinguish session date validation failures","messageBody":"Report malformed components, impossible calendar dates, and past dates separately so trainers can correct the actual error. Keep execution-time validation and the User Guide consistent, with independent regression cases for each failure.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":19,"deletions":18},"docs":{"insertions":3,"deletions":1},"test-code":{"insertions":18,"deletions":6}}},{"hash":"4d00a150445aecf1c2e6628175997558c16f5a01","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Reuse client name matching for session commands","messageBody":"Expose the existing whitespace normalization through Name and use a common full-name matcher for duplicate checks and session lookup. Reuse the same normalization in parsing and sort ties so the rules cannot drift apart.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":20,"deletions":7},"test-code":{"insertions":20,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"649a2cc99e0f5c56729141777de7d6c9357760a9","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Preserve sessions and measurements together","messageBody":"Integrate the original measurement commits from PR #67 with the next-session feature. Use one full Person constructor carrying both fields so bookings, measurements, contact edits and JSON reloads retain all client data.\n\nAdd mixed-feature regression coverage for replacement in both directions, displayed indices, legacy JSON and failed-save rollback. Verified 366 tests, Checkstyle, coverage generation, the MarkBind build, repository checks and both card rows in JavaFX.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"57e06f92d15acecb1a9b914bb9dcc2f4b1f92ee8","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge master and preserve client training records","messageBody":"Integrate the merged add/delete and persistence features with sessions and measurements. Preserve the address removal, optional email, list validation, Spotter branding and data-change-only saving from master while retaining both training fields in client copies, edits and JSON storage.\n\nUnify the filter accessor for failed-save rollback and verify the mixed-feature workflow for clients without email. Validation: 391 tests, Checkstyle, coverage, shadowJar, MarkBind, repository checks and an offscreen card smoke test pass.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"f23e9a0986a8a18908d1d09e1443d0b